# =============================================================================
# Repo-root .dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The client production image (client/Dockerfile.prod) builds with the REPOSITORY
# ROOT as its build context (it COPYs both client/ and Deploy/client-nginx.conf),
# so the context would otherwise sweep in every lane's node_modules, build output,
# and local state. Keep the context lean and prevent host artifacts (incl. any
# local .env with real secrets) from ever entering an image layer.
#
# NOTE: each COPY in the Dockerfiles is explicit (client/package.json, client/,
# Deploy/client-nginx.conf), so this file is defense-in-depth + build-speed, not
# the sole guard. server/ and services/kiwi/ build from their own lane contexts
# and have (or should have) their own ignores; this root file governs the
# repo-root-context client build.
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies / build output (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
client/.vite

# Secrets + local env — MUST never enter an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
Deploy/nginx.conf
**/*.tar

# Python / loader caches (not needed by the client image)
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/*.pyc
tools/ingest/output
db/_work

# Local images / backups / blobs
Deploy/backups
**/var/images
server/var

# VCS + editor + OS noise
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*Zone.Identifier

# Tests / coverage (not needed at image build)
**/coverage
**/.pytest_cache

# Process/handoff docs live OUTSIDE Repository/, but guard anyway
**/REVIEW_*.md
**/FIX_REPORT_*.md
